depgraph: build the dep_check() result directly for lists without a choice

Sub-series: G (flat dependency lists) - patch 1 of 1; applies to 3.0.83 with only the earlier patches of this sub-series.

For a dependency list that is a non-empty list of plain Atoms only (no
"||" group, no virtual/, nothing from package.provided, local_config, no
virt_parent), dep_check() has nothing to choose: it returns every atom in
order. _select_atoms_flat() builds that result directly, including the
OrderedDict keyed by the parent that _select_atoms_highest_available()
returns, and dep_check() is not called.

On top of patches 0001-0019, resolve seconds before -> after
(median of the runs, at least 2 per figure):
  start 26.9 -> 25.7, holds 13.6 -> 12.9, masks 28.7 -> 27.2,
  py313 17.0 -> 15.8, bdeps 19.7 -> 18.5, policykit 13.9 -> 13.2
  sum of six 119.8 -> 113.3 (-6.5 s, -1.5 % of the stock sum 447.5)
Patches 0001-0020 together: 447.5 -> 113.3 s (-75 %); 447.5 is the
stock sum of the ladder run of 2026-11-20, stock was not run again here.

Weak spots and what was not checked:
* Same dependence on dep_check() internals as the previous point, here for
  the whole result including its order.

Origin: written by AI agents (Claude) in the emerge-fast job, 2026-11-17..20;
